For the coarse realized-signature poset `P` and fiber profiles `B_p`, define the lexicographic fiber expansion

`F = sum_{p in P} B_p`.

Then every refinement factors canonically as

`Q -> F -> P`,

where `Q -> F` is same-vertex descent thinning and `F -> P` is fiber expansion/projection. After T0, all `B_p` are singletons, so `F ~= P` and only thinning remains.

